{"summary":"This pull request introduces a ProfileHeader component that computes and displays a user's full name via useState and useEffect. This pattern introduces unnecessary state synchronization and causes extra render cycles.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":[],"assumptions":["No PR description was provided, so intent was inferred solely from the diff."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/profile/ProfileHeader.tsx","line":6,"endLine":10,"evidence":"const [fullName, setFullName] = useState("");","title":"Store derived values directly instead of using state and effects","why":"Storing derived data in state with an effect causes an extra render pass on every prop change and adds unnecessary state synchronization overhead.","fix":"Derive the full name directly during render instead of syncing it into state via useEffect.","suggestedCode":"export function ProfileHeader({ firstName, lastName }: Props) {
  const fullName = `${firstName} ${lastName}`;
  return <h1>{fullName}</h1>;
}","category":"react","kind":"improvement","severity":"medium","confidence":0.95}]}

