      query: (body) => ({ url: "/entries", method: "POST", body }),
      invalidatesTags: ["Entry"],
    }),","category":"api","kind":"bug","severity":"high","confidence":0.95}]}

{"summary":"The PR introduces a new RTK Query API slice for the timesheet feature with endpoints for fetching and adding entries. However, the mutation endpoint lacks cache tag invalidation, which will cause the UI to show stale data after adding an entry.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":["Clean and idiomatic use of RTK Query createApi structure."],"assumptions":["The /entries endpoint returns the newly created entry or invalidation is needed so getEntries refetches."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/timesheet/timesheetApi.ts","line":13,"endLine":15,"evidence":"    addEntry: build.mutation<Entry, NewEntry>({","title":"Missing cache invalidation on addEntry mutation","why":"When a new timesheet entry is successfully added via mutation, the cached entries list will not be invalidated. As a result, the UI will not automatically refetch or display the new entry until a manual page reload.","fix":"Add invalidatesTags: ['Entry'] to the addEntry mutation definition to ensure the cache is invalidated and getEntries automatically refetches.","suggestedCode":"    addEntry: build.mutation<Entry, NewEntry>({
      query: (body) => ({ url: "/entries", method: "POST", body }),
      invalidatesTags: ["Entry"],
    }),","category":"api","kind":"bug","severity":"high","confidence":0.95}]}
